<title>LITHUANIA: BOURSE CAPITALISATION DOWN.</title>
<headline>BOURSE CAPITALISATION DOWN.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The capitalisation of the</p>
<p>Vilnius bourse dipped to 5.697 billion litas last Friday versus</p>
<p>5.786 billion litas a week earlier, the National stock exchange</p>
<p>said on Monday.</p>
<p>Vilnius bourse staistics:</p>
<p>					     April 07-11   April 01-04</p>
<p>    Submitted orders		   13,697	  11,029</p>
<p>    Executed orders		    1,580	   1,210</p>
<p>Number of transaction on</p>
<p>    central market (CM)		1405	    1,102</p>
<p>    Turnover on the CM in LTL	11,534,000    7,158,160</p>
<p>Number of transactions in</p>
<p>    bloc trades (BT)		   88		54</p>
<p>    Turnover of BT in LTL	    21,677,020    11,652,690</p>
<p>    Supply of shares per week	39,457,808    33,860,222</p>
<p>    Demand of shares per week	4,083,278     2,980,627</p>
<p>Turnover of shares</p>
<p>    on CM per week in LTL	    7,292,490     7,158,160</p>
<p>    in BT per week in LTL	    19,654,910    11,652,690</p>
<p>The number of transactions</p>
<p>    in government T bills	    17		0</p>
<p>The turnover of government</p>
<p>    T-bills in LTL per week	  6,263,620     0</p>
<p>--Andrius Vilkancas, Vilnius newsroom + 370 2 22 35 17</p>
